## Products

### Polygon PoS
Polygon PoS is Ethereum's most-used sidechain and the primary settlement layer for stablecoin payments. It provides high-throughput, low-cost transactions with Ethereum-anchored security. Sub-cent fees, 2-second finality, and 2,100+ TPS as of early 2026. The Gigagas roadmap targets 100,000 TPS.
- URL: https://polygon.technology/polygon-pos
- Docs: https://docs.polygon.technology

### Polygon AggLayer
AggLayer is Polygon's cross-chain aggregation protocol that unifies multiple ZK-powered blockchains into a single liquidity and interoperability layer. It allows users, businesses, and AI agents to send and receive money across different chains as if they were all on one network.
- URL: https://www.agglayer.dev

### Polygon CDK
Multistack toolkit for building ZK-powered, high-performance chains. Used by enterprises and developers to launch custom Layer 2 or Layer 3 chains with Polygon's security and tooling.
- URL: https://www.agglayer.dev/cdk-enterprise

### Polygon Vaultbridge
Turns TVL into sustainable, chain-native revenue. Enables chains to generate yield from their own liquidity.
- URL: https://www.agglayer.dev/agglayer-vaultbridge

### POL Token
POL is the native utility and governance token of the Polygon ecosystem. Used for staking to secure the Polygon network, governance participation, and gas fees. POL replaced MATIC as part of the Polygon 2.0 upgrade and is MiCA-compliant under EU crypto-asset regulations.
- POL overview: https://pol.polygon.technology
- MiCA Whitepaper: https://polygon.technology/pol-micar-whitepaper

