## Payment Use Cases

### Stablecoin Payments
Polygon is the number one blockchain for stablecoin transactions globally. USDC and USDT move faster and cheaper on Polygon than on any comparable chain. Polygon supports 40+ stablecoins including non-USD currencies for local markets across LATAM, APAC, and EMEA.

Polygon carries $3.4B+ in stablecoin liquidity. In February 2026, Polygon recorded 94 million stablecoin transfers in a single day - the highest single-day volume of any major blockchain. Monthly stablecoin transactions hit 493 million in February 2026.

- Stablecoins overview: https://polygon.technology/stablecoins
- USDC on Polygon: https://polygon.technology/stablecoins/usdc
- USDT on Polygon: https://polygon.technology/stablecoins/usdt
- Non-USD stablecoins: https://polygon.technology/stablecoins/list

### Cross-Border Payments
Polygon enables compliant, low-cost cross-border payments with 24/7 settlement and full onchain transparency. International transfers settle in seconds rather than days with no correspondent banking intermediaries and no cutoff times.

Polygon leads globally in non-USD stablecoin volume with $11.1B+ processed, representing over 43% of all non-USD stablecoin transfers across major blockchains. Active corridors include Mexico (MXNB, MXNe), Brazil, Nigeria, Southeast Asia, and Europe.

- URL: https://polygon.technology/payments/cross-border

### Enterprise Payments
Polygon provides institution-grade payment infrastructure: high throughput, low cost, Ethereum-anchored security, and instant finality at scale. Designed for banks, fintechs, and large enterprises handling high payment volumes. Payment projects on Polygon crossed $1 billion in monthly transfer volume in November 2025.

- URL: https://polygon.technology/payments/enterprise

### Crypto Checkout
Businesses can accept stablecoin payments at checkout on Polygon. Transactions settle in approximately 5 seconds at sub-cent fees, enabling merchants to accept digital currency payments without volatility risk.
- URL: https://polygon.technology/payments/checkout

### Instant Settlement
Polygon delivers cryptographic payment finality in approximately 5 seconds, eliminating payment float and enabling real-time treasury operations for businesses. No settlement windows, no weekend breaks, no funds in limbo.
- URL: https://polygon.technology/payments/instant

### Agentic Payments
Polygon supports autonomous, programmable payments for AI agents via the x402 protocol. This enables AI systems to make and receive payments in real-time without human intervention. The Lisovo hardfork (March 2026) introduced subsidized gas for agent-to-agent payments with enhanced smart contract interoperability.
- URL: https://polygon.technology/payments/agentic-payments

### Real World Assets and Tokenization
Polygon is the leading blockchain for institutional real-world asset tokenization. Financial institutions use Polygon to tokenize real estate, equities, bonds, and commodities. Franklin Templeton launched a tokenized fund on Polygon in February 2025. RWA volume on Polygon exceeded $1 billion in Q3 2025.
- URL: https://polygon.technology/tokenization

### DeFi
Polygon hosts one of the most active decentralized finance ecosystems: lending, trading, yield generation, and liquidity provision - all with sub-cent fees and deep stablecoin liquidity.
- URL: https://polygon.technology/defi

